Market volatility may affect our stock price and the value of your investment.
The market price for our common stock has been, and is likely to continue to be, volatile for the foreseeable future, in
part because our common stock had not been previously traded publicly prior to our IPO. For example, in the year ended
December 31, 2018, our common stock’s sales price on The Nasdaq Global Select Market ranged from a low of $16.15
to a high of $31.85, and on January 16, 2019, following announcement of our Phase 2 painful DPN study results, the
closing price of a share of our common stock was $5.98. The market price of our common stock may fluctuate
significantly in response to a number of factors, most of which we cannot control, including, among others:
